.TH FASTRDPCTL 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdpctl \- query and control the fastrdp session broker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdpctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.B status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B fastrdpctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.B tickets
.RI [ user ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B fastrdpctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.B logout
.I user
.br
.B fastrdpctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.B clear\-grace
.RI [ user ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastrdpctl
talks to a running
.BR fastrdp-brokerd (8)
over its admin socket.
.TP
.BR status " [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
List the sessions known to the broker, the Kerberos TGT of each account with a
session (see
.BR tickets )
and the broker's counters (connections, pending tokens, MFA reconnect grace entries).
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print the broker's reply as JSON instead of tables.
.TP
.BR tickets " [\fIuser\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
Show the TGT in the default credential cache of each account with a session, or of
.I user
(a local account, with or without a session): principal, cache, expiry and renewal
limit (UTC, with the time left) and a state:
.B ok
(renewable for more than 24 hours),
.B expiring
(expires within 1 hour),
.B not_renewable_soon
(not renewable, or renewal ends within 24 hours: the user must log in again with a
password, or run
.BR kinit ),
.B expired
(the user has lost Kerberos access, e.g. to Kerberized NFS homes),
.B none
(no TGT: login without a password, such as SSO or smartcard),
.B unknown
(klist failed or timed out).
The broker runs
.BR klist (1)
with the user's ids and without
.BR KRB5CCNAME ,
so it sees the cache the user's session uses (default_ccache_name, normally KCM:).
Only metadata is shown, never ticket or key data.
.TP
.BI logout " user"
Terminate all sessions of
.IR user .
.TP
.BR clear\-grace " [\fIuser\fR]"
Forget the MFA reconnect grace
.RB ( "[mfa] reconnect_grace" )
of
.I user
(the local account name, as in the broker log), or of all users. Their next
login asks for the second factor again. Use it on a suspected compromise, together
with
.BR logout .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " config\fR, " \-\-config " config"
Broker configuration file (default
.IR /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml ),
used to find the socket.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-brokerd (8),
.BR klist (1),
.BR sssd-kcm (8)
